# Days of Miracles and Wonder - 2026 Update
After Paul Simon - The Boy in the Bubble (Graceland, 1986) - original line: "These are the days of miracles and wonder"
Date: 2026-09-30
Format: one stanza per line

These are the days of miracles and wonder / And don't cry baby, don't cry, don't cry
It was a slow day / And the feed was beating / On the scrollers in the checkout line / There was a rocket / Landing backwards in Texas / While a chatbot wrote a lullaby
These are the days of miracles and wonder / This is the long-distance call / The way the camera follows us in slo-mo / The way we look to us all
Our telescopes seeing first light / Baby pictures from the edge of time / We got CRISPR scissors splicing codons / And mRNA in record time / We got taxis with no drivers in Phoenix / Real-time translation on a phone / Fusion flashing twice in Livermore / And black holes photographed - unknown, now known
It was a slow day / And the grid was humming / On the solar roofs in summer heat / There was a robot / Folding proteins in seconds / What took grad students years to complete
These are the days of miracles and wonder / This is the late-night lab report / The way the model dreams in language / The way we teach it, short and short
We got dishes talking to the far side / Startup landers bouncing on the Moon / We got midnight launches out of Mahia / We got rain maps made by balloon / We got voices cloned from three seconds / We got fake and real in the same frame / We got cures for sickle cell approved / And the climate models calling names
It was a dark day / And the sirens were wailing / Over Kharkiv in the winter black / There were hunters / That never blink or sleep / And they find their mark every time
These are the days of lasers in the data center / Lights that stitch the world to all / Staccato signals of constant information / And your phone says "baby, don't cry, don't cry" / These are the days of miracles and wonder / Don't cry baby, don't cry, don't cry

## Footnotes - alternatives per stanza

[1] Chorus opener. Alt: "These are the days of miracles and wonder / Don't cry baby, don't cry, don't cry" (drop And, tighter). Alt: keep Simon's "wonder" singular for rhyme with "under". Alt: swap baby for darling if too retro.

[2] Slow day / feed / rocket. Alt setup: "It was a slow day / And the queue was buzzing / At the depot for the night bus home". Alt rocket: "There was a booster / Caught by chopsticks in Texas" (Mechazilla catch). Alt chatbot: "While a model wrote a lullaby" (less product-y than chatbot). Alt: "While the fridge reordered milk" for mundane contrast.

[3] Long-distance call chorus. Alt: "This is the stutter-step of time / The way the signal bends to us all". Alt: lean into video-call era: "This is the Zoom that never ends". Alt: keep slo-mo but swap "camera follows us" for "camera loves us".

[4] Telescopes / CRISPR / taxis / fusion / black holes. LOCKED: "Our telescopes seeing first light" over "We got..." for flow + double meaning (engineering first light + cosmological First Light). LOCKED A: "We got CRISPR scissors splicing codons" over "rewriting code" (code = Python confusion, codons = erudite, 11 syllables, splicing = correct verb). Alt CRISPR: "CRISPR shears re-spelling codons" (more hymnal, drop we got). Alt mRNA: "And CAR-T in record time" or "And sickle-cell cured by design". Alt taxis: "We got no-driver cabs in Austin" if Phoenix dates it. Alt fusion: "Stars lit twice in Livermore" (more sacred than flashing). Alt black holes: "And shadows photographed - M87, now known".

[5] Slow day / grid / protein robot. LOCKED: "On the solar roofs in summer heat" (best diction, avoids on-solar smear, summer as proverb). Alt: "On solar roofs in summer heat" (8 syllables, leanest, universal, staccato delivery needed). Alt: "On solar roofs in India's heat" (proper-noun global, India heatwave + solar rollout, vivid but steps forward). Alt grid: "And the panels were drinking / On the rooftops in the midday heat". Alt robot: "There was a folder / Dreaming proteins in seconds" (AlphaFold nod). Alt: "What took PhDs ten years to complete" if grad students too soft.

[6] Lab report chorus. Alt: "This is the overnight training run". Alt: "The way the model talks in its sleep". Alt: drop "short and short", try "taught and taught" or "prompt and prompt" for LLM in-joke.

[7] Dishes / landers / launches / voices / cures. Alt dishes: "We got ears on the far side" (Queqiao relay). Alt landers: "Bargain landers bouncing on the Moon" (startup = cheap). Mahia = Mahia Peninsula, North Island NZ, Rocket Lab Launch Complex 1 (Electron). Chosen over Vandenberg / Cape for off-radar poetry, but obscure. Alt Mahia: swap for "Vandenberg" if Mahia too obscure, or "Mahia at midnight" explained in liner. Alt voices: "We got dead voices back in three seconds" (darker, Villa-Lobos demo vibe). Alt fake/real: "We got true and false in the same frame". Alt cures: "We got Casgevy by design" (brand name, erudite).

[8] Closer / lasers in data center. Alt: "These are the days of lasers in the desert" (Vegas sphere / heliostat nod). Alt: "Staccato signals" is Simon's original, keep as homage. Alt ending: "And your feed says baby, don't cry" (phone -> feed, more 2026). Alt: end cold on wonder, no repeat.
